---
/*
  Traduction anglaise de histoire-de-radio-odyssey.astro (§81, lot 2).

  ⚠️ Page factuelle sur des personnes et des dates réelles. Chaque fait ici
  vient de la version française : 12 août 1994, Pas-de-Calais, fréquence FM
  temporaire, Winamp et Raduga, mise en sommeil de plus de 25 ans, retour le
  19 janvier 2025, nom inspiré du groupe Odyssey. Ne rien y ajouter de
  mémoire, et corriger ici si la version française est corrigée.

  Les liens sortants ne pointent que vers des pages anglaises. Elisabeth
  Bélot-Grimaud est nommée mais pas liée : sa page n'existe qu'en français.
*/
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Sidebar from '../../components/Sidebar.astro';
import FAQBlock from '../../components/FAQBlock.astro';
import RelatedPages from '../../components/RelatedPages.astro';

const faq = [
  { q: 'Has Radio Odyssey always been an online station?', a: "No. The association was founded on 12 August 1994 in the Pas-de-Calais region of northern France, broadcasting on FM — including a temporary frequency granted for a local commercial fortnight. It then lay dormant for more than 25 years, returning on 19 January 2025, this time exclusively online." },
  { q: 'Why did it stop broadcasting for all those years?', a: "For a very ordinary reason: the two founders' professional careers took over from the association. Radio Odyssey stayed dormant until its return in 2025." },
  { q: 'Is the partnership with the psychologist a recent thing?', a: "No — that meeting predates the station's return by several years. It was a conversation about wellbeing and heart coherence breathing that directly triggered the relaunch in January 2025." },
  { q: 'Where does the name "Radio Odyssey" come from?', a: "From the American band Odyssey and their track \"Going Back to My Roots\", in the 80s." },
];
---
<Layout
  lang="en"
  altLangs={{ fr: '/histoire-de-radio-odyssey.html', en: '/en/the-story-of-radio-odyssey.html' }}
  title="The Story of Radio Odyssey | From 1994 FM to Today"
  description="Founded in 1994 by two radio enthusiasts in northern France, dormant for 25 years, back online in 2025 with heart coherence breathing. The full story."
  articleDatePublished="2026-08-16"
>
  <PageHero
    gradientFrom="#FFD700"
    gradientTo="#0b1c2d"
    homeLabel="🏠 Home"
    homeHref="/en.html"
    breadcrumbCurrent="The story of Radio Odyssey"
    title="The Story of Radio Odyssey"
    text="From an association founded in 1994 in northern France to the web radio of today — a little over 30 years, told by its programme director."
  >
    <Fragment slot="icon">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="17" stroke="white" stroke-width="2.2"/><path d="M24 15V24L30 28" stroke="white" stroke-width="2.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"/></svg>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <main class="ro-section" data-pagefind-body>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row gy-4">
        <div class="col-lg-8">

          <div class="content-card">
            <p style="margin:0;">Radio Odyssey was not born in 2025. Long before it became the positive, breathing-friendly web radio you can hear today, it existed on FM, in the Pas-de-Calais region of northern France, more than 30 years earlier. Here is that story, as told by its programme director.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>1994: two enthusiasts meet</h2>
            <p>The Radio Odyssey association was founded on <strong>12 August 1994</strong> by two radio enthusiasts — one drawn to the high-frequency engineering side, the other to broadcasting itself. Each had been experimenting separately with transmitters and shows when chance brought them together, and Radio Odyssey came out of that meeting. A few months later, the association was even granted a temporary FM frequency, for a local commercial fortnight.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>Where the name comes from</h2>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">It was inspired by the American band <strong>Odyssey</strong> and their track <em>"Going Back to My Roots"</em>, in the 80s.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>The early technical days: from Winamp to Raduga</h2>
            <p>In the 90s, computers were only just arriving in radio. Radio Odyssey was already using Winamp to play mp3 files — genuinely radical at a time when stations were still cueing up CDs. For scheduling, the association relied on <strong>Raduga</strong>, which made it possible to run a professional music station with ad breaks inserted automatically — very useful during the temporary FM period. Nobody ever measured the audience of those years: that was never the point.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>A long dormancy, then an unexpected return</h2>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">The two founders' professional careers eventually took over from the association, and Radio Odyssey went quiet for more than 25 years. It came back — online only — on <strong>19 January 2025</strong>. That return was no accident.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>The meeting that actually caused the relaunch</h2>
            <p>The 2025 return grew out of a much earlier meeting with Elisabeth Bélot-Grimaud, a doctor of cognitive psychology, and a conversation about wellbeing and heart coherence breathing. One of them had the tools and the radio knowledge; the other had the expertise on subjects that were becoming more and more prominent. <em>"What if we teamed up and made a radio station with heart coherence breathing in it?"</em> On 19 January 2025, Radio Odyssey became a web radio — carrying, from day one, the same positive programming it already had in the 90s, long before that stance became a trend.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>What changed, and what didn't</h2>
            <p>More than 25 years separate the two eras of Radio Odyssey. A great deal changed — and yet, not so much:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>The signal no longer travels 20 km on FM: it is hosted on a streaming platform and can be heard anywhere in the world with an internet connection</li>
              <li>The mixing desk, the CD decks and the dedicated computer have given way to an entirely file-based chain</li>
              <li>mp3 is still here, but digital compression quality has improved enormously since the 90s</li>
              <li>The software changed, but the underlying principle — a music schedule that is thought through, not left to chance — has not</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="content-card">
            <h2>One thing we're proud of</h2>
            <p>In a little over eighteen months since the relaunch, Radio Odyssey has built a website, a proper app, and a base of regular listeners. But the real pride lies elsewhere: putting a heart coherence breathing sequence on air at the top of every hour, all day long, inside a bright and positive music schedule — and claiming it openly as the station's signature. As far as we know, that combination is unique in France, and quite possibly beyond. Radio Odyssey is now carried by the main international web radio platforms.</p>
          </div>

          <FAQBlock items={faq} idPrefix="en-story" lang="en" />

          <RelatedPages
            lang="en"
            alsoLike={[
              { href: '/en/what-makes-radio-odyssey-different.html', label: 'What Makes Radio Odyssey Different', desc: 'The mission and the choices behind it' },
              { href: '/en/heart-coherence-breathing-radio.html', label: 'Heart Coherence Breathing Radio', desc: 'The signature sequence, explained' },
              { href: '/en/music-for-a-better-mood.html', label: 'Music for a Better Mood', desc: 'Our positive-radio philosophy' },
            ]}
            associated={[
              { href: '/en/radio-odyssey-faq.html', label: 'Radio Odyssey FAQ' },
              { href: '/en/free-radio-no-ads-no-sign-up.html', label: 'Free Radio, No Ads, No Sign-Up' },
              { href: '/en/80s-throwback-radio-online.html', label: '80s Throwback Radio Online' },
            ]}
          />

          <div class="page-cta-bar">
            <h3>Hear the result, live</h3>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.8rem;justify-content:center;margin-top:1rem;">
              <a href="#" onclick="roPlayNow(event)" class="btn-hero">
                <Icon name="broadcast-pin" /> Listen to Radio Odyssey
              </a>
              <a href="/en.html" class="btn-hero-ghost">
                <Icon name="house-door-fill" /> English home
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-4">
          <Sidebar lang="en" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
